Defines the rules for when and how invoices should be paid (due dates, installments, discounts), applied automatically on sales orders, invoices, and vendor bills.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Standard terms: 30/60/90 days net, immediate payment
Split payments (e.g. 30% advance + 70% on delivery)
Early payment discounts (2% 10 days, net 30)
Applied on customer invoices, vendor bills, and sales/purchase orders
Controls due date calculation and aging reports
Fiscal compliance (localization-specific terms)

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), active (boolean)
line_ids → One2many to account.payment.term.line (most important)
company_id
note (html for invoice footer)
Computed: due_date calculation logic

Critical child model: account.payment.term.line
value (percent/balance), days, value_amount, discount_days, discount_percentage

Critical Hooks: compute, _compute_terms, onchange for line recalculation
Security: Basic company rules (accessible to sales & accounting users)

RAG Routing Keywords:
payment term, payment terms, terms and conditions, due date, net 30, 2/10 net 30, installment, early discount, payment schedule, invoice due date, split payment, payment condition
Related Models (most joined):

account.payment.term.line (child lines)
account.move (via invoice_payment_term_id)
sale.order, purchase.order
account.move.line (for due date on lines)
res.partner (default payment term)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.payment.term defines customer and vendor payment conditions with name and multiple account.payment.term.line for installments, days, percentages, and early payment discounts. It is used to automatically compute due dates on invoices (account.move), sales orders, and purchase orders, driving aging reports, cash flow forecasting, and financial compliance across Odoo sales, purchase, and accounting modules.